                  <provenance type="#b e"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_268">Hyde (Hida, formerly
                        New Minster, Winchester), Hampshire. Benedictine abbey of Holy Trinity, St
                        Mary the Virgin, and St Peter</orgName><p>Medieval binding: label on back
                        with 'HVDA' and 'Opus domini Roberti lincolniensis Grosthedi' (s. xv),
                        secured by a metal border fastened by 8 nails. Centre strap and clasp marks,
                        also two other strap-attachment marks above and below the centre of first
                        board. Chain attachement top of first cover in centre.</p><p>Fragment of
                        kalendar of Hyde abbey (s. xii ex.) in binding contains first 17 days of
                        August (Oswald in blue, Assumptio in blue, Inventio s. Stephani, Laurence
                        red, Ethelwold black) and 16 days of July (2--17) (Swithun black, Grimbald
                        red, Transl. s. Benedicti and Oct. of Peter and Paul blue, Sexburg, Hedda
                        and Kenelm black).</p></provenance>
